// =============================================================================
// buying-terms-course — "Buying: Price, Terms and the Count to Finish"
// =============================================================================
// Course three of the Real Estate department, and the first one BETWEEN its two
// ends: DR-0500 built the footing (whose the ground is) and DR-0501 the capstone
// (how it is run). This one covers the transaction itself, which is where a
// believer most often gets quietly compromised -- not by a crime, but by a
// lawful practice nobody names.
//
// THE ARC, one argument in eight moves:
//   1. Abraham refused the gift and paid in public (Genesis 23:13, 16, 18)
//   2. Two sets of weights in one bag (Deuteronomy 25:13, 15; Proverbs 11:1; Micah 6:11)
//   3. It is naught, it is naught, saith the buyer (Proverbs 20:14)
//   4. Surety: the trap you talk yourself into (Proverbs 6:1-5; Proverbs 11:15)
//   5. Haste is the most expensive thing in the deal (Proverbs 21:5; 28:20, 22)
//   6. What borrowing makes you, and what it does not (Deuteronomy 15:6; Romans 13:8)
//   7. Give a portion to seven, and also to eight (Ecclesiastes 11:2)
//   8. He that sweareth to his own hurt, and changeth not (Psalms 15:4; Numbers 30:2)
//
// Pay honestly -> one standard -> speak truly -> guarantee nothing you cannot
// time -> verify before you close -> know what borrowing makes you -> keep
// portions against what you cannot foresee -> keep your word when it costs.
// Lesson 8 is last on purpose and says so: integrity at the hard moment is
// mostly the accumulated result of the seven decisions before it.
//
// THE RECURRING SHAPE, named across three courses now: a defect that is
// invisible from inside any single instance. The false weight (each deal
// defensible alone), the lawful process that took Naboth's vineyard (every step
// wore a form), and attrition on a promise (every delay defensible). The
// department teaches the same eye three times, on three different objects.
//
// NO PASSAGE IS SHARED with the department's other courses, and the course test
// CHECKS that against their own reference lists rather than trusting it.
//
// AGE BANDS FROM THE FIRST COMMIT (DR-0497 / DR-0498): every lesson carries
// levels.teen and levels.senior, authored rather than re-registered.
//
// VERIFICATION (DR-0076 / SCRIPTURE-REFERENCE-STANDARD). All 67 quoted spans
// were fetched VERBATIM from the repository's own KJV. The generator caught two
// elisions inside quotations in the first draft; DR-0459 forbids them and the
// only remedy is a shorter genuinely-verbatim span, so each became two real
// spans. Our prose says Yahweh; quotations keep "the LORD" exactly as the KJV
// has it (DR-0210's bright line).
//
// TEACHING, NOT LEGAL OR FINANCIAL ADVICE -- carried on the meta. Lesson 6 in
// particular states both edges of what the Word says about borrowing and stops
// where Scripture stops (DR-0098): it is not called sin, and it is not
// flattered.
// =============================================================================

