    bigIdea: 'The commandment is about what you carry, not only what you do: "Thou shalt not have in thy bag divers weights, a great and a small" (Deuteronomy 25:13). A heavy weight to buy with and a light one to sell with — each transaction defensible on its own, and the pair of them a fraud. Yahweh calls the instrument itself an abomination: "A false balance is abomination to the LORD: but a just weight is his delight" (Proverbs 11:1). And Micah asks the question that ends the argument, aimed at the bag rather than the deal: "Shall I count them pure with the wicked balances, and with the bag of deceitful weights?" (Micah 6:11).',
